## 4. Form Builder & Creation

### A. Fetch Field Types Blueprint
Before rendering the drag-and-drop form builder, fetch the exact schema blueprints for all supported field types. This tells your frontend exactly what configuration sidebars to render!

**Request:** `GET /api/forms/field-types/`
**Response:**
```json
[
  {
    "category": "Basic",
    "types": [
      {
        "name": "number",
        "label": "Numeric input",
        "description": "",
        "properties_schema": {
          "min": "number",
          "max": "number",
          "decimals": "boolean"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

### B. Draft a Form
Save a draft of the form schema under a project.

**Request:** `POST /api/projects/<project_uuid>/forms/`
```json
{
  "title": "Pothole Survey",
  "description": "Daily tracking of road defects.",
  "schema": {
    "fields": [
      { "name": "road_name", "type": "text", "label": "Road Name" },
      { "name": "location", "type": "point", "label": "GPS Coordinates" },
      { "name": "photo", "type": "image", "label": "Defect Photo" }
    ]
  }
}
```

### C. Fetch & Edit Form Structure (Schema)
If the web app needs to display or edit an existing form's questions, you can fetch the full form detail, which includes the current `schema`. 

**Request:** `GET /api/forms/<form_uuid>/`
**Response (abridged):**
```json
{
  "id": "65fa6507...",
  "title": "Pothole Survey",
  "status": "draft",
  "current_version_details": {
    "schema": {
      "fields": [
        { "name": "road_name", "type": "text", "label": "Road Name" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

To update the form questions, send a `PATCH` request with the new `schema` object:
**Request:** `PATCH /api/forms/<form_uuid>/`
```json
{
  "schema": {
    "fields": [
      { "name": "road_name", "type": "text", "label": "Road Name" },
      { "name": "severity", "type": "number", "label": "Severity (1-10)" }
    ]
  }
}
```

### D. Publish Form (Crucial Step!)
Forms are just drafts until they are published. Publishing triggers the backend to dynamically generate a dedicated, spatial PostGIS table (e.g., `collect_pothole_survey_a1b2c3d4`) to store the submissions.

**Request:** `POST /api/forms/<form_uuid>/publish/`

